---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { aiReadinessHonestyLine } from '../data/visibilityReport';
---

<Layout
  title="FAQ — Rank Labs GEO & SEO Services, Pricing & Plans"
  description="Frequently asked questions about Rank Labs GEO/SEO services. How AI-powered GEO and SEO works, pricing, plans, and getting started."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-28 pb-16 sm:pt-32 sm:pb-24">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold gradient-text mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-400 mb-12">Everything you need to know about AI-powered GEO/SEO with Rank Labs.</p>

    <!-- FAQPage Schema -->
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={`{
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does Rank Labs differ from a traditional SEO agency?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Rank Labs is built around continuous execution, not occasional recommendations. We audit your site every week, resolve eligible technical issues, track search rankings and your AI Optimization score, identify content opportunities, and report exactly what changed, including the leads we can track. With Full Management, we also maintain your website, publish approved content, and manage business listings—so the work moves from analysis to implementation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What's included in the Rank Labs Visibility Report ($399/mo)?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The Rank Labs Visibility Report is a report-only, month-to-month report covering SEO + AI Optimization (on-page). It includes Google organic and Maps (local pack) rankings for 25 keywords, the keywords you rank for, a backlink summary, a full technical crawl, Core Web Vitals, schema, sitemap/robots, SSL and email-domain (DNS) setup checks, an AI Optimization on-page score with sub-scores for ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude and Perplexity covering schema, direct-answer structure and AI-crawler access (on-page signals), business-detail conflict checks on Google, Bing, Apple Maps, Facebook, Yelp, BBB, Yellow Pages, Foursquare, MapQuest, and Angi or one industry directory, reviews on Google plus one other site, and a 3-competitor comparison. With your access, it can optionally include GA4, Google Search Console, and Google Business Profile stats. You get a weekly SEO audit report email plus a separate monthly email report (first week of each month). You handle all fixes — Rank Labs makes no changes to your site. See the full list. Want us to do the work? Upgrade to Full Management ($1,249/mo)."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What's included in Full Management ($1,249/mo)?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Full Management includes weekly site audits (100+ checks), keyword rank tracking, weekly AI Optimization on-page scoring, and monthly reports — and we implement the fixes — plus: complete site hosting on Cloudflare Pages, blog approval pipeline (drafts → you approve → we publish), internal link architecture optimization, business listing management (Google Business Profile, Bing Places), conversion-focused A/B testing, service-area landing pages, and priority same-day fix processing. A 6-month contract gets the first month free and the $999 migration fee waived; otherwise it is month-to-month plus a $999 migration fee."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How quickly will I see results?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "SEO is a long-term strategy. Most customers see measurable ranking improvements within 3–6 months. Our weekly audits catch issues immediately — broken links, missing tags, and crawl errors are fixed within days, not months. Your monthly report also shows the leads we can track, so you can see whether the work is turning into customers."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need to know anything about SEO?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not with Full Management, which is fully managed. We handle all technical SEO, content creation, and reporting. You receive clear, jargon-free weekly reports showing your site's health score, keyword rankings, and what was improved. If something needs your attention, it's clearly explained in plain English. With the Rank Labs Visibility Report, the report is in plain English too, but you (or your team) implement the fixes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is GEO (Generative Engine Optimization)?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "GEO is preparing your site so AI assistants like ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, and Perplexity can read, trust, and quote it. Traditional SEO is about ranking in Google's results; GEO is about being a clear, citable source for AI answers. Our reports include an AI Optimization on-page score with a sub-score per assistant. ${aiReadinessHonestyLine} ASO (Agentic Search Optimization) goes one step further: making your business the one an AI can actually pick and book."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is ASO (Agentic Search Optimization), and is it the same as App Store Optimization?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "ASO stands for Agentic Search Optimization, and we also call it being \\"agent-ready.\\" It's the work that gets your business chosen by an AI assistant that's actually doing something for a customer — not just mentioned in an answer. GEO makes you easy to quote; ASO makes you easy to choose. And no, it is not the same as App Store Optimization — that \\"ASO\\" is a completely different discipline from the app world. Ours is about being the business an AI agent selects when it's asked to compare options and take the next step."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What's the difference between GEO and ASO?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "GEO (Generative Engine Optimization) makes your content easy for AI to quote. ASO (Agentic Search Optimization) makes your business easy for AI to choose: hours, prices, location, services, and a booking link published as data. Much of the groundwork is shared (schema markup, accurate business details, AI-crawler access). GEO adds the content layer; ASO adds the action layer."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What does \\"agent-ready\\" actually mean for my business?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Being agent-ready is a ladder, not a switch. Level 0 — Invisible: no structured data. Level 1 — Identified: a machine can tell who you are and where. Level 2 — Screenable: it can answer the routine questions (hours, prices, quality, service area). Level 3 — Reachable: there's a machine-usable way to start a booking or enquiry. Level 4 — Verifiable: a machine can tell whether you actually have openings. Level 5 — Transactable: the agent completes the booking end to end. For most businesses, the highest-return work sits at Levels 3 and 4."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is ASO included in my plan?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Agent-readiness implementation is part of Full Management. Full Management implements it — machine-readable hours, exact-price offer markup, a published booking entry point, and an availability signal — all deployed and maintained for you. The Rank Labs Visibility Report ($399/mo) includes an AI Optimization score but is report-only: you handle all fixes, and Rank Labs makes no changes to your site."
          }
        },
